            <div class="col-sm-8">
                <h2>Air Compressor Repair</h2>
                <p>
                    Portland Compressor offers two types of air compressor repair - both inside service where you can bring your compressor to us (ideal for homeowner, portable, wheelbarrow and lightweight air compressors) and outside service, where our trained and certified technicians drive to your location. Outside service is great for stationary reciprocating and rotary screw air compressor system. Our outside compressor service technicians travel all throughout the state of Oregon and SW Washington. See our 
                    <a href="@Url.Action("CompressorService", "Compressor")">air compressor service</a> area.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Also available are <a href="@Url.Action("Maintenance", "Compressor")">preventative maintenance</a> plans, where our service technicians inspect filters, oils, belts, etc... in order to ensure that all components are up to date. This service can be completed as often as the customer would like, but is generally performed either quarterly or bi-annually. For the most current rates, please call our service dept. at 1-866-208-5646.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Both our inside and outside compressor repair options are able to perform similar services. Common repairs include replacing and servicing pumps, filters and regulators, pressure switches and belt replacements. Also available are oil changes and checkups to ensure that your equipment is up to date and eliminates downtime.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
                <h2>Airless Paint Sprayer Repair</h2>
                <p>
                    One of the most common placement parts on an airless sprayer is the internal packings. When the <a href="~/store/airless-sprayer-packing-kits">packings</a> are clean and in good working order, you get the performance that you would expect from your airless sprayer. When packings start to wear, often times your sprayer will have trouble priming and pushing paint to the gun. As this continues, your piston rod, cylinder and other internal parts will start to break down as well. Fortunately, our inventory is vast and our paint sprayer repairmen have the experience that you need to keep your sprayer in good working order.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Whether it is a simple repack or the replacement of a prime valve, we have the resources to help eliminate your downtime. We are one of the nations largest independent paint sprayer distributors, and are an authorized service center for Graco, Titan, Wagner, SprayTech, Speeflo, Campbell Hausfeld, and other major sprayer brands.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Outside of regular airless paint sprayers, we are also able to service <a href="@Url.Action("Trouble_Shooting", "TextureSprayers")">texture paint sprayers</a>,
                    <a href="@Url.Action("trouble_shooting", "HVLP")">HVLP fine finish</a> units, and <a href="@Url.Action("LineLazerTroubleShooting", "stripers")">line stripers</a>. For additional information on the types of paint sprayers that we are able to service and repair, call our service department at 1-866-208-6087
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-4">
